<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>7.7.4: Relate the Domain of a Function to Its Graph</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01855</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.7.4: Relate the Domain of a Function to Its Graph</md:title>
    <md:uuid>9538278a-71a7-4c62-8084-adbd243be166</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section>
      <para>This graph represents the revenue in dollars that a company expects if they sell their product for \(p\) dollars.</para>
      <para>
        <figure>
          <media alt="Graph of non linear function.&quot; height=&quot;196">
            <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_09_09_01.svg"/>
          </media>
        </figure>
      </para>
      <section class="check-understanding">
        <title>Cool Down Activity</title>
        <exercise id="_7df5f3e7-792b-4438-a54b-e9a7d2660cd7" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Based on this model, which price would generate more revenue for the company, \($5\) or \($17\)?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! \($5\), as it would generate about \($3,700\) in revenue. Charging \($17\) would bring in about \($2,500\). </para>
            <para>Incorrect. The correct answer is \($5\), as it would generate about \($3,700\) in revenue. Charging \($17\) would bring in about \($2,500\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
      <section class="check-understanding">
        <exercise id="_91a80edb-e118-490e-9da1-3a90f3dac2be" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
            <para>At what price (in dollars) should the company sell their product if they wish to make as much revenue as possible?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! Based on the graph, a price of \($10\) would bring in the most revenue.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \(10\). Based on the graph, a price of \($10\) would bring in the most revenue.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="dd50d498-c21d-414b-ad51-cdebc7560f33" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
            <para>How much revenue (in dollars) would they make?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! Based on the graph, a price of \($10\) would bring in about \($5,000\).</para>
            <para>The correct answer is \($5,000\). Based on the graph, a price of \($10\) would bring in about \($5,000\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
      <example>
        <exercise>
          <problem>
            <para>What is an appropriate domain for the function? Explain how you know.</para>
            <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Compare your answer: Your answer may vary, but here is a sample.</para>
            <para>\(0 \leq p \leq 20\), because the price has to be non-negative, and the company would earn negative revenue if the price were more than \($20\).</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </example>
    </section>
  </content>
